WEBVTT

00:03:28.547 --> 00:03:30.447
So let's move to the brain.

00:03:31.383 --> 00:03:34.774
Now, here we have a brain.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.961
This is donated by a social scientist,

00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:43.580
and they said they didn't know what
it was or indeed, how to use it, so --

00:03:43.604 --> 00:03:46.558
(Laughter)

00:03:46.582 --> 00:03:47.743
Sorry.

00:03:48.714 --> 00:03:50.294
So I borrowed it.

00:03:50.318 --> 00:03:52.006
I don't think they noticed. OK.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.594
(Laughter)

00:03:54.618 --> 00:03:57.791
The point I'm trying to make
is that when you're asleep,

00:03:57.815 --> 00:03:59.559
this thing doesn't shut down.

00:03:59.583 --> 00:04:02.265
In fact, some areas of the brain
are actually more active